# Test-harness-only entry file — see ../real-stack/Caddyfile.real-stack.test /
# ../stubs/Caddyfile.test for why a global options block cannot arrive via
# `import` from snippets/ (it must be the very first thing in the file Caddy
# actually loads). `local_certs` switches Caddy to its own internal CA:
# api.tapiz-reload.test is a reserved, non-issuable TLD with no real ACME path,
# exactly like the other two harnesses' `.test` hostnames.
#
# Unlike the other two harnesses, this file imports sites from a LOCAL
# `sites-live/` directory (a live, bind-mounted COPY of the real
# `sites/tapiz.caddy`, refreshed by run.sh before every reload) rather than the
# repo's real `sites/` directly — see run.sh step 8 for why: the graceful
# reload proof in this harness needs to mount a config directory it can safely
# overwrite mid-run with a harmless, then a broken, edit, without ever touching
# this repository's real `sites/tapiz.caddy` file. `snippets/` is still the
# real, unmodified repo directory (never edited by this harness).
{
	local_certs
}

import snippets/*.caddy
import sites/*.caddy
